<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diego de Vargas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1643–1704</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Diego de Vargas was a Spanish governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-mexico">New Mexico</a> who led its reconquest after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pueblo-revolt">Pueblo Revolt</a> of 1680. In 1692 he reoccupied Santa Fe largely without bloodshed, and in 1693 he returned with settlers, retaking the city by force when its Pueblo occupants resisted. He was governor again from 1703 and died on campaign against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apache">Apache</a> in 1704.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diego-de-vargas.jpg" alt="Diego de Vargas" width="320" height="618" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ddevargas.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
